    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Kyle Tucker** (77.32) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Kyle Tucker** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Michael Lorenzen\u2019s 4.71 xERA and a solid order position. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** draws a high-velocity threat in Zac Gallen, but his elite efficiency stems from a 100% stolen base expectation against a slow-working battery, making him an invaluable asset in our quest to win the scarcest category. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also projects as a top-tier start, as he is currently exploiting a significant platoon advantage against Tatsuya Imai, with his #2 spot in the order providing ample opportunities to drive up our runs and RBI totals.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung** (53.27), who fell just shy of our rotation due to the depth of our infield options. While **Josh Jung** carries a respectable projection, he was displaced by the higher-scoring dynamic platoons of **Curtis Mead** and **Coby Mayo**, both of whom benefit from favorable matchups today. We are also closely monitoring the weather in the **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** games, as a 44% rain risk puts their availability in jeopardy. Despite the risk, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to his lead-off role, though his matchup against Matthew Boyd is complicated by a negative platoon shift. Owners should keep a close eye on final lineup confirmations for **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**, as their projected efficiency is sensitive to their specific spot in the order, which could pivot their total scores significantly if they fall out of the premium spots.",
